.TH PWD 1 "30th of July 2026" zenithutils "User Commands"

.SH NAME
pwd - print path of working directory

.SH SYNPOSIS
\fBpwd\fP \fI[-LP]\fP

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBpwd\fP prints full path the current working directory

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB-L\fP
use PWD environment variable instead of libc functions

.TP
\fB-P\fP
dereference any symlinks

.PP
Note: \fB-P\fP is the default
.PP
Note: This program may possibly never run, given it is usually built into the shell
